ARM64EC: Preserve copy-on-write protection while tracking executable pages.

Keep COW intervals distinct from ordinary writable code for SMC fault recovery,
query results and bulk protection changes. Track image, data-map, DEP promotion
and free/unmap transitions. Otherwise an executable COW map is reported as RWX
and a later write can repeatedly fail when FEX requests shared-write access.

